  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Expression for an electric field is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>4000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;The electric flux through the cube of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> when placed in electric field (as shown in the figure) is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"assets\\qt0104_fbc35287031d.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 297px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "640",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Electric flux is expressed as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is area of the surface and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;the angle between the electric field lines and the normal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.</p><p>The flux will be only from DEFG surface as on the surface OABC field is zero&nbsp;and for rest of the surface, area vector is perpendicular to field.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0104_23ac48925699.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 274px;\" /></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4000</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4000</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>640</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>"
  }
}